    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The rest of the syllabary",
     "texto": [
      "With these rows you have all 46 basic signs.",
      "The **h** is breathed out: は is «ha», a very soft breath. But ふ is **fu**: you blow between your lips, without biting your lip as you do for English «f».",
      "The Japanese **r** is just one quick tap of the tongue, like the tt in \"butter\", never strong, like a rolled r.",
      "The **y** and **w** rows are incomplete: only や, ゆ, よ and わ, を.",
      "ん is a standalone **n**: it is the only sign that has no vowel."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
