    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Three tricky signs",
     "texto": [
      "を is pronounced the same as お («o») and is only used as a particle.",
      "は is read «ha» inside a word, but when it is a particle it is read **wa**. That is why こんにちは is said «konnichiwa».",
      "へ is read «he», but when it is a particle it is read **e**. You will see particles very soon."
     ],
